*---------------------------------------------------------------
* kdisp.equ -- the kernel dispatch-table length.
*
* HOISTED OUT OF kdisp.s (S9 L4, 2026-08-30). Merlin-8's `ENT`
* exports code labels only -- an EQUATE cannot cross the linker
* -- so a constant two REL modules both name has to be shared at
* ASSEMBLY time, through a put file. Equates emit nothing, so
* the move is byte-neutral; check-bytes is the proof.
*---------------------------------------------------------------
*
* IT IS A BOUND, NOT A COMMENT. entry.s refuses any call number
* above it, so a handler wired into kdisp.s's table without
* raising this number is unreachable -- and the refusal is
* silent and indistinguishable from a handler that ran and
* declined (2026-09-21: SYS_HALT's first run printed its own
* "kernel refused" line and returned to the prompt).
K_DISP_COUNT equ 26     ;26: SYS_SLPUNTIL (docs/SLEEP-1.md);
                        ;25 was SYS_VROOT (docs/VROOT.md),
                        ;appended after SYS_DEVLIST
